W: 1. Bonny Charlie's noo awa'
W: Safely o'er the friendly main,
W: Mony a heart will break in twa,
W: Should he ne'er come back again.
W:
W: Chorus:
W: Will ye no come back again?
W: Will ye no come back again?
W: Better lo'ed ye canna be.
W: Will ye no come back again?
W:
W: 2. Ye trusted in your hieland men,
W: They trusted you dear Charlie!
W: They kent your hiding in the glen,
W: Death and eile braving.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 3. English bribes were a' in vain
W: Tho' puir and puirer we maun be,
W: Siller canna buy the heart
W: That aye beats warm for thine and thee.
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 4. We watched thee in the gloamin' hour
W: We watched thee in the mornin' grey,
W: Though thirty thousand pounds they gi'e,
W: Oh, there is nane that would betray!
W: (Chorus:)
W:
W: 5. Sweet's the laverock's note and lang,
W: Liltin' wildly up the glen
W: But aye to me he sings a sang,
W: "Will ye no come back again?"
W: (Chorus:)
